{% from "design-system/components/section-title.njk" import sectionTitle %}
{#
  PATTERN C — a grid of N equal columns, 4-across on desktop and 2-across on mobile.

  Same two ingredients as pattern A: MJML columns + `fluid`. The only extra is the mobile width —
  `.step-col` re-asserts 50% inside the shared mobile block's territory, because "stack to ONE
  column" (the `.fluid` default) would make four short cards very tall for no reason. That rule
  lives in this email's own <mj-style> (see index.mjml.njk), not the shared head, because no other
  email has a step strip.

  Nunjucks loops the steps; the width (25%) is authored, not computed. If you add a fifth step it
  wraps to a second row on its own — which is the MJML behaviour you want, and the reason not to
  compute widths from the array length.
#}
{$ sectionTitle('WHAT HAPPENS NEXT', tokens) $}
<mj-section padding="16px 20px 4px 20px">
  {% for step in content.nextSteps %}
  <mj-column css-class="step-col fluid" width="25%" vertical-align="top" padding="8px 6px">
    <mj-text align="center" padding="0 0 10px 0">
      {# Numbered disc. Width/height as HTML ATTRIBUTES as well as CSS: the Gmail app ignores CSS
         sizing on a <td> that has no attribute and collapses the disc to the text box.

         The numeral is NAVY on the pastel chip, not orange. Orange-on-pastel is the design system's
         one genuinely unreadable pair — 2.70:1, below even WCAG AA-large — and at 14px it washed out
         to the point the step numbers were guesswork. Navy on the same chip is 8.68:1 and keeps the
         pastel-orange language intact; only the digit colour changes. See docs/tokens.md. #}
      <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" align="center" width="34" style="margin:0 auto;width:34px;">
        <tr><td width="34" height="34" style="width:34px;height:34px;background-color:{$ tokens.color.orangeSoftBg $};border-radius:999px;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle;font-family:{$ tokens.font.stack $};font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:{$ tokens.color.navy $};">{$ step.step $}</td></tr>
      </table>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text css-class="step-title" align="center" color="{$ tokens.color.heading $}" font-size="13px" font-weight="700" line-height="1.3" padding="0 0 5px 0">{$ step.title $}</mj-text>
    <mj-text align="center" font-size="12px" line-height="1.5" color="{$ tokens.color.muted $}" padding="0">{$ step.desc $}</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
  {% endfor %}
</mj-section>
